    delphi:hasScore "0.635"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The surface family and claimed parameter continuum yield clear geometric model comparisons. Available public imagery likely tests some species but is insufficient for the asserted complete graded series." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Build calibrated 3D outlines of Vorticella bells, fit partial unduloids under the measured stalk and ciliary-ring boundaries, and compare fits with alternative constant-mean-curvature and flexible surfaces. Map fitted parameters across species to test for a continuous cylinder-to-sphere gradation." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Most public images are 2D and not taxonomically balanced.", "Live contraction changes bell shape.", "Species identification and boundary-ring dimensions may be missing." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch05-17--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch05-17--gpt--dataset-2> .
